  "contract": "[68A4,68BC) is the next level-setup fragment: BSR 6A94, LEA FF0690,A5, BSR 6EB6, LEA FF0838,A5, BSR 6EB6. 6A94 clears 16 x 12 bytes from FF447A, FF31AC and FF31B0, then for each of 16 FF312C kinds that is not FFFF calls 6AF0 with D2 = kind, D3 = the FF314C count, D0/D1 = the next FF4C80 pair (Y + 16), A3 = the next FF447A record and A0/A1 = that entry's addresses. 6AF0 pops an F9E2 object, stores A5 at +4A and A3 at +42, writes the (object, A0, A1) record, mode 81, position, extents 0010/0010, frames by 6B44 (signed kind < 14: kind*6 + 0260 by MULU.W/ADDI.W, end +5; else 020D/0205 families or 01FD), service 6BD6, countdown D3 and cadence by 6BB2 (1/1 when the count is 2, else 5/5), handler 12646; only the target is inherited. 6EB6 pops one object, stores it at +1A2 of the A5 control record and clears its mode (dormant, 6EC8's shape). Native requires verified inheritance and zero unrepresented bytes, else rejects with no change. Exhaustion enters the never-returning FA1E loop. 6BD6's hit path 6C00 and the later setup from 68BC are not reconstructed."
